    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Como ver o trace de uma execução",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "O `trace_id` de cada execução vem no evento `run.started` e no cabeçalho `X-Trace-ID` das respostas HTTP. Abra a tabela abaixo ou [explore os traces no Tempo](/explore?schemaVersion=1&orgId=1&panes=%7B%22a%22%3A%7B%22datasource%22%3A%22tempo%22%2C%22queries%22%3A%5B%7B%22refId%22%3A%22A%22%2C%22datasource%22%3A%7B%22type%22%3A%22tempo%22%2C%22uid%22%3A%22tempo%22%7D%2C%22queryType%22%3A%22traceql%22%2C%22query%22%3A%22%7Bresource.service.name%3D%5C%22getnet-support-api%5C%22%20%26%26%20name%3D%5C%22run%5C%22%7D%22%7D%5D%2C%22range%22%3A%7B%22from%22%3A%22now-1h%22%2C%22to%22%3A%22now%22%7D%7D%7D) e cole o `trace_id` em *Explore > Tempo > TraceID*. Os logs estruturados (Loki) trazem o mesmo `trace_id`."
      }
    },
